ers/yelloweennnn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yelloweennnn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yelloweennnn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yelloweennnn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yelloweennnn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yelloweennnn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T21:32:55Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T21:32:55Z","body":"I believe this addresses a separate issue, I'm happy to discuss if I'm missing something.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3403692541/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3405509568","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108175#issuecomment-3405509568","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108175","id":3405509568,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7K-_PA","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T09:41:30Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T09:41:30Z","body":"> I believe this addresses a separate issue\n\nI don't think so. The VM crash is caused by legitimate compiler optimizations. The problem lies with the static analyzer. We allow users to omit the return type when implementing a native virtual method or overriding a custom method due to compatibility and the gradual typing design of GDScript (static typing is optional). When you explicitly specify the return type, the analyzer checks covariance, but when you don't specify it at all, the analyzer doesn't check type compatibility at all.\n\nWe can't simply force users to always specify the return type if the parent method has one. This would violate the gradual typing design and break compatibility by forcing users to always specify the type when implementing a native virtual method or overriding a custom method, which users of dynamically typed GDScript may not want (for example, if you're overriding a class method from an addon or library).\n\nThe proper approach, in my opinion, is to keep track of the type even if it's not explicitly stated. Example:\n\n```gdscript\nclass A:\n    func f() -> int:\n        return 0\n\nclass B extends A:\n    func f(): # `-> int` is not required.\n        return \"\" # But this produces an error.\n\nfunc _ready(): # `-> void` is not required.\n    return 123 # But this produces an error.\n```\n\nHowever, we may also need runtime checks if the analyzer cannot prove type safety (but I think this case is already taken into account and will not require further action if we provide the correct type to the compiler).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3405509568/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3405984384","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108175#issuecomment-3405984384","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108175","id":3405984384,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LAzKA","user":{"login":"notroid5","id":87585310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NTg1MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87585310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5","html_url":"https://github.com/notroid5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T11:38:42Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T11:38:42Z","body":"Updated to still be reproducible in 4.5 and added a comment in the second example since it also works without the static typing of the variable\n\nAlso, this issue is about returning functions that have a static return type themselves, especially if it is already predefinded like in this case with `randf`. No one should be forced to use static typing but GDScript should use the information is has. It should be possible to forward the type, right?\n\nI don't see how the three examples are related to this, either I misunderstand @dalexeev or vice versa?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3405984384/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3406117359","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108175#issuecomment-3406117359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108175","id":3406117359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LBTnv","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T12:17:02Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T12:17:02Z","body":"> I don't see how the three examples are related to this, either I misunderstand [@dalexeev](https://github.com/dalexeev) or vice versa?\n\nSorry, I didn't read the description carefully and haven't re-read it since. Indeed, this is a different bug, and I don't know if it's related to the one I mentioned. I've seen this bug before but almost forgot about it since #90694 pushed it out of my memory. 